					'9.1 Si applica esclusivamente il diritto svizzero, con esclusione della Convenzione di Vienna (CISG). Restano riservate le disposizioni imperative di protezione dei consumatori del paese di domicilio del cliente.',
					'9.2 Il foro competente è Biel/Bienne, Canton Berna. Per i consumatori vale inoltre il foro legale del loro domicilio (art. 32 CPC).',
					'9.3 Se una disposizione delle presenti CG fosse invalida, le altre restano valide.',
					'9.4 secondsurf può modificare queste CG in qualsiasi momento. Per un ordine vale la versione pubblicata sul sito al momento dell’ordine.',
				],
			},
		],
	},
	en: {
		subtitle: 'secondsurf.ch – Second-hand surf clothing',
		note: 'This translation is for information only. The German version is the binding one (section 2.5).',
		updated: 'Last updated: 5 November 2026',
		sections: [
			{
				title: '1. Scope and provider',
				paragraphs: [
					'1.1 These general terms and conditions (terms) apply to all orders placed through the online shop www.secondsurf.ch.',
					'1.2 The provider and contracting party is: {owner}, secondsurf.ch, Biel/Bienne, Canton of Bern, Switzerland, email: {email} (hereinafter “secondsurf” or “we”).',
					'1.3 The offer is aimed at private customers (hereinafter “customer”). Separate conditions, which we send on request, apply to resellers and wholesale customers.',
					'1.4 The version of these terms valid at the time of the order applies. Different conditions of the customer only apply if we agree to them in writing.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: '2. Offer and conclusion of the contract',
				paragraphs: [
					'2.1 The presentation of items in the online shop is not a binding offer but an invitation to order.',
					'2.2 By submitting the order with the “Buy now” button, the customer makes a binding offer. Before that, they can check and correct their details at any time.',
					'2.3 After successful payment, the customer receives an order confirmation by email. The purchase contract is concluded with this confirmation.',
					'2.4 Almost all items are one of a kind. If an item is bought more than once through simultaneous orders, the order paid first applies. Other customers are informed and receive a full refund of the amount paid.',
					'2.5 The language of the contract is German.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: '3. Prices and payment',
				paragraphs: [
					'3.1 All prices are final prices in Swiss francs (CHF). secondsurf is not registered for VAT, so no VAT is shown. Shipping costs are shown separately before the order is completed.',
					'3.2 Payment is made through the payment provider Stripe. Depending on what the checkout offers, credit and debit cards, TWINT, Apple Pay or Google Pay are available.',
					'3.3 Payment is due when ordering. Payment details are processed directly by Stripe; secondsurf does not store any card information.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: '4. Delivery and shipping',
				paragraphs: [
					'4.1 We deliver within Switzerland and to Liechtenstein with Swiss Post. Shipping costs {price} per order; from an order value of {free}, shipping is free.',
					'4.2 Orders are usually shipped within 2 working days of receiving payment. Stated delivery times are not binding.',
					'4.3 Deliveries to the EU are only possible on request. The customer contacts us before ordering by email at {email}. We tell them the shipping costs and conditions in advance. Customs, import duties and foreign taxes are paid by the customer. Mandatory consumer protection rights of the customer’s country of residence remain reserved.',
					'4.4 The risk passes to the customer when the goods are handed over. If a parcel arrives visibly damaged, we ask the customer to inform us immediately with photos.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: '5. Second-hand goods and condition',
				paragraphs: [
					'5.1 secondsurf sells used clothing. Every item is checked, cleaned and described with its condition (e.g. “very good”, “good”, “some wear”). Visible defects are shown in the description and the photos.',
					'5.2 Normal signs of wear and defects mentioned in the description are not a defect within the meaning of the warranty.',
					'5.3 Colours may differ slightly from the picture depending on the screen. Sizes are taken from the original label; where possible we also give measurements.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: '6. Returns',
				paragraphs: [
					'6.1 Under Swiss law there is no statutory right of withdrawal for online purchases. As almost all items are used one-of-a-kind pieces, we do not take back or exchange goods without defects.',
					'6.2 A return is possible if the customer received the wrong item, the item was damaged in shipping or it does not match the description:',
					[
						'The customer tells us within 14 days of receipt using the form at {returns} or by email at {email}, with photos if possible.',
						'The customer sends the item back in the condition they received it in.',
					],
					'6.3 We pay for the return shipping and refund the purchase price and shipping costs within 14 days to the original payment method. If the customer prefers, they receive a gift card of the same value instead. Further rights under the warranty (section 7) remain reserved.',
					'6.4 For deliveries to the EU, the mandatory withdrawal rights of the country of residence also apply, in particular the 14-day right of withdrawal for consumers.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: '7. Warranty',
				paragraphs: [
					'7.1 The statutory provisions apply (Art. 197 ff. Swiss Code of Obligations). As the goods are used, the warranty period is one year from delivery (Art. 210 para. 4 CO).',
					'7.2 The customer checks the goods on receipt and reports recognisable defects immediately, at the latest within 7 days, by email with photos. Hidden defects are reported as soon as they are discovered.',
					'7.3 In the case of a justified defect, we refund the purchase price against return of the goods or grant an appropriate price reduction, as the customer chooses. As the items are one of a kind, replacement with an identical item is usually not possible. We pay the cost of returning a defective item.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: '8. Liability and data protection',
				paragraphs: [
					'8.1 secondsurf is liable without limitation for damage caused intentionally or through gross negligence. Liability for slight negligence is excluded to the extent permitted by law.',
					'8.2 We are not liable for delays or losses caused by the transport company, disruptions of the payment provider or force majeure, to the extent permitted by law.',
					'8.3 We process personal data in accordance with the Swiss Data Protection Act. Details are in our privacy policy at {privacy}.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: '9. Final provisions',
				paragraphs: [
					'9.1 Swiss law applies exclusively, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods (CISG). Mandatory consumer protection provisions of the customer’s country of residence remain reserved.',
					'9.2 The place of jurisdiction is Biel/Bienne, Canton of Bern. For consumers, the statutory place of jurisdiction at their place of residence also applies (Art. 32 Swiss Civil Procedure Code).',
					'9.3 Should a provision of these terms be invalid, the remaining provisions remain valid.',
					'9.4 secondsurf may change these terms at any time. An order is governed by the version published on the website at the time of the order.',
				],
			},
		],
	},
};
const c = content[lang];
---

<LegalPage
	lang={lang}
	title={t('legal.terms')}
	description={{
		de: 'AGB von secondsurf: Bestellung, Preise, Zahlung, Versand, Rückgabe und Gewährleistung.',
		fr: 'CGV de secondsurf : commande, prix, paiement, livraison, retour et garantie.',
		it: 'Condizioni generali di secondsurf: ordine, prezzi, pagamento, spedizione, resi e garanzia.',
		en: 'Terms of secondsurf: ordering, prices, payment, shipping, returns and warranty.',
	}[lang]}
>
	<p class="subtitle">{c.subtitle}</p>
	{c.note && <p class="note">{c.note}</p>}
	{
		c.sections.map((section) => (
			<>
				<h2>{section.title}</h2>
				{section.paragraphs.map((p) =>
					Array.isArray(p) ? (
						<ul>
							{p.map((item) => (
								<li set:html={fill(item)} />
							))}
						</ul>
					) : (
						<p set:html={fill(p)} />
					),
				)}
			</>
		))
	}
	<p class="updated">{c.updated}</p>
</LegalPage>

<style>
	.subtitle,
	.updated {
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}
	.note {
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
		background: var(--accent-tint);
		font-size: var(--step--1);
	}
	.updated {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		font-size: var(--step--1);
	}
</style>
